  "summary": "Shinran, born in Kyoto in 1173, was a Buddhist priest who became a disciple of Honen and founded the Jodo Shinshu (Shin) school. After years in the Kanto region spreading the nenbutsu teaching, he returned to Kyoto and devoted his last decades to writing. Sources give his death as 1262 or 1263.",
